DataLens — multi-tenant natural-language querying
=================================================

This distribution contains:

1. The `vanna` library (`backend/vanna/`), derived from the upstream project at
   https://github.com/vanna-ai/vanna, Copyright (c) Vanna.AI, MIT licensed.

   Modified here. The substantive additions are the semantic layer
   (`backend/vanna/semantic/`), the datasource registry
   (`backend/vanna/core/datasource/`), the ranked retrieval index
   (`backend/vanna/capabilities/index/`), the dashboards package
   (`backend/vanna/dashboards/`), the billing plans
   (`backend/vanna/core/billing/`), and the authentication primitives
   (`backend/vanna/core/auth/`).

   Two upstream surfaces have been removed, neither of them imported by anything
   in this distribution:

     - the `vanna.legacy` package -- the 0.x compatibility layer, roughly eleven
       thousand lines covering twenty-five vendor integrations;
     - the developer command line and its example gallery (`vanna.cli`,
       `vanna.examples`, `vanna.skills`, and the Flask/MCP/CLI server runners),
       along with the vector-store agent-memory backends that the multi-tenant
       control plane replaces with its own.

2. The DataLens application (`backend/vanna_app/`), which is a multi-tenant
   deployment of that library: control plane, accounts, billing, and the HTTP
   surface over them. Original to this repository, MIT licensed on the same terms.

3. The database schema (`database/`): numbered migrations applied under an
   advisory lock, and the generated schema dump and configuration seed.

4. Front-end assets (`frontend/`): the workspace page, the operator console, and
   the `<vanna-chat>` web component.

   `backend/vanna/dashboards/vendor/tile-figure.js` is a deliberate copy of
   `frontend/public/assets/shared/tile-figure.js` so that a server-rendered
   dashboard export and the live page draw a tile identically. The copies are
   asserted byte-identical by the test suite and synchronised by
   `make plotly-bundle`.

   `backend/vanna/dashboards/vendor/plotly-export.min.{js,css}` is a custom
   Plotly build, Copyright (c) Plotly, Inc., MIT licensed, produced from
   `backend/tools/plotly_export_bundle/`.

See LICENSE for the terms, which apply to all of the above.

Third-party Python dependencies are declared in `backend/requirements.in` and
pinned in `backend/requirements.txt`; front-end dependencies are declared in
`frontend/package.json` and pinned in `frontend/package-lock.json`. Each carries
its own licence.
